1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,001
Jesus asked three fishermen for one thing.

2
00:00:02,541 --> 00:00:03,662
They failed inside an hour.

3
00:00:03,782 --> 00:00:04,382
Gethsemane.

4
00:00:05,322 --> 00:00:06,303
The night before the cross.

5
00:00:06,823 --> 00:00:09,144
tarry ye here, and watch with me.

6
00:00:09,364 --> 00:00:10,344
Then he stepped away to pray.

7
00:00:11,005 --> 00:00:14,966
O my Father, if it be possible, let this cup

8
00:00:15,106 --> 00:00:20,229
pass from me: nevertheless not as I will, but

9
00:00:20,489 --> 00:00:21,869
as thou wilt.

10
00:00:22,429 --> 00:00:24,450
And he cometh unto the disciples, and findeth

11
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:27,712
them asleep, and saith unto Peter, What, could

12
00:00:27,732 --> 00:00:29,612
ye not watch with me one hour?

13
00:00:29,853 --> 00:00:30,333
Not a curse.

14
00:00:31,133 --> 00:00:32,314
A diagnosis full of mercy.

15
00:00:32,794 --> 00:00:36,495
Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation:

16
00:00:37,496 --> 00:00:40,957
the spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh

17
00:00:41,397 --> 00:00:41,878
is weak.

18
00:00:42,098 --> 00:00:43,478
He returned to the same prayer.

19
00:00:43,598 --> 00:00:45,579
The cup he asked to pass, he drank.

20
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:47,160
On the cross.

21
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:48,661
For you.

22
00:00:48,781 --> 00:00:50,581
So bring him the weak flesh he already knows.

23
00:00:51,642 --> 00:00:53,362
When you cannot watch, pray anyway.

24
00:00:53,943 --> 00:00:54,863
He is watching.

25
00:00:54,943 --> 00:00:56,164
He watched that hour alone.

26
00:00:57,204 --> 00:00:58,945
Now no hour of yours is watched alone.
